/-!
# Integrality shape for the weight-m floor Riemann–Roch space

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.isIntegral_and_isIntegral_of_mem_riemannRochSpace_weightFloor`
(`4378864a-6bf6-50e9-8e4b-cdec05b41d44`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `bd45be07-b3b5-53c4-9f93-daac2a14f55b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field and let $F$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over
$K$. Let $y \in F$ be an element whose image in $K((q))$ is the series [`ModularCurve.jqModC
K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the power
series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum`; assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable
over the intermediate field $K(y)$ generated by $y$. Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $D$ be a divisor
on $F/K$, i.e. a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places $w$ of $F/K$ (valuation
subrings of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$, and principal ideal rings), such that for every
$w$, $D(w)$ is the sum of $(2m\,\mathrm{ord}_w y)/3$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w y > 0$ and $0$ otherwise,
$(m\,\mathrm{ord}_w(y-1728))/2$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w(y-1728) > 0$ and $0$ otherwise, and
$m\,\mathrm{ord}_w y$ when $\mathrm{ord}_w y < 0$ and $0$ otherwise; here $\mathrm{ord}_w$ is minus
the logarithm of the adic valuation at $w$, and the quotients are integer division, hence floors for
these non-negative numerators. Let $G \in F$ lie in the Riemann–Roch space of $D$, i.e. $w(G) \le
\exp(D(w))$ for every place $w$. Then, writing $j$ for [`ModularCurve.jqModC
K`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) and viewing $G$ in $K((q))$: $G^6 j^{4m}(j-1728)^{3m}$ is
integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $G^2 j^{m}(j-1728)^{m}$ is integral over the
$K$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$.

This is the level-free form of the statement that an element of the weight-$m$ floor Riemann–Roch
space has the integrality (holomorphy) shape of a weight-$2m$ modular function on the two standard
charts of the $j$-line, the two conjuncts being integrality over $K[j]$ and over $K[j^{-1}]$. It is
used in the proofs of the lower bounds for the dimensions of spaces of modular forms of even and of
odd weight on $\Gamma_1$.

